[" Here is an example of a JavaScript function that fulfills the given requirements:

```javascript
class DOMTraverser {
  constructor(selector, apiUrl, cache = new Map(), cloneFunction = Object.assign) {
    this.selector = selector;
    this.apiUrl = apiUrl;
    this.cache = cache;
    this.cloneFunction = cloneFunction;
  }

  async traverse(rootElement, callback = () => {}) {
    const visitedNodes = new Set();

    const queue = [rootElement];

    while (queue.length > 0) {
      const currentNode = queue.shift();

      if (!visitedNodes.has(currentNode)) {
        visitedNodes.add(currentNode);

        let matchedElements = [];

        // Check if the node matches the specified selector
        if (currentNode.matches && currentNode.matches(this.selector)) {
          matchedElements.push(currentNode);
        } else if (currentNode.shadowRoot) {
          const shadowRootMatchedElements = await this.traverse(currentNode.shadowRoot, callback);
          matchedElements = matchedElements.concat(shadowRootMatchedElements);
        }

        // Traverse through child nodes and custom elements
        Array.from(currentNode.children).forEach((child) => queue.push(child));
        Array.from(currentNode.getElementsByTagName('*')).forEach((taggedChild) => queue.push(taggedChild));

        // Integrate with an external API to fetch additional metadata for each element
        const promises = matchedElements.map(async (element) => {
          if (!this.cache.has(element)) {
            const cacheKey = `${element.outerHTML}${Date.now()}`;
            const cachedData = await (async function () {
              try {
                const response = await fetch(`${this.apiUrl}/${encodeURIComponent(cacheKey)}`);
                return await response.json();
              } catch (error) {
                console.warn(`Error while fetching metadata for ${element}:`, error);
                return null;
              }
            }.bind(this));

            this.cache.set(element, cachedData);
          }

          return this.cache.get(element);
        });

        const metadata = await Promise.all(promises);

        callback(matchedElements, metadata);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Usage example:

```javascript
const traverser = new DOMTraverser('.my-selector', 'https://your-api.com/metadata');
traverser.traverse(document.body, (matchedElements, metadata) => {
  // Do something with the matched elements and their metadata here
});
```

The above code provides a basic structure for a DOM traverser function that can efficiently collect elements matching a specified selector from a potentially complex DOM structure, including shadow DOM and custom elements. It also integrates with an external API to fetch additional metadata for each element and implements a caching mechanism to mitigate repeated API calls.

You can adjust the balance between initial load time and memory footprint by modifying the cache size or the API function's behavior according to your specific use case. Keep in mind that you may need to optimize further based on actual performance requirements and test under different scenarios."]

[" here's a simplified implementation of your requirements using ES6 modules, Promises, and some common JavaScript techniques.

```javascript
class Loader {
  constructor(options = {}) {
    this.basePath = options.basePath || '';
    this.fileTypeExtensions = options.fileTypeExtensions || ['.js', '.json'];
    this.sequenceLength = options.sequenceLength || 3;
    this.log = options.log || console.log;
  }

  async load(filename) {
    const filenameParts = filename.split('.');
    let fileExtension = filenameParts.pop();

    if (!this.fileTypeExtensions.includes(fileExtension)) {
      fileExtension = this.determineFileExtension(filename);
    }

    const loadedFilename = this.prependSequenceNumber(filename, this.sequenceLength);
    const loadedFilePath = `${this.basePath}/${loadedFilename}${fileExtension}`;

    try {
      let response;
      if (/^http/.test(loadedFilePath)) {
        response = await fetch(loadedFilePath);
      } else {
        response = await import(`${loadedFilePath}`);
      }

      return response.default || response;
    } catch (error) {
      this.log(`Error loading file ${loadedFilename}:`, error.message);
      throw error;
    }
  }

  determineFileExtension(filename) {
    const extensionRegex = /\.([a-zA-Z0-9]+)$/;
    const match = filename.match(extensionRegex);

    if (match && match[1]) return match[1];

    let extension = '';

    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
      extension = filename.substring(i, i + 1).toUpperCase();
      switch (extension) {
        case 'J':
        case 'A':
        case 'V':
        case 'A'.repeat(this.sequenceLength):
          return '.js';
        default:
          continue;
      }
      break;
    }

    return '';
  }

  prependSequenceNumber(filename, length) {
    let sequence = '';
    for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) {
      sequence += Math.floor(Math.random() * 10);
    }

    const filenameParts = filename.split('.');
    const baseName = filenameParts.slice(0, -1).join('.');

    return `${sequence}${baseName}.${filenameParts[filenameParts.length - 1]}`;
  }
}
```

Usage:

