  // Do something with the loaded module
});

// Load remote file
loader.load('https://cdn.example.com/script.js').then(module => {
  // Do something with the loaded module
});
```"]

['```java
import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.ConcurrentSkipListMap;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.Optional;
import java.util.function.Consumer;
import java.util.stream.Stream;

public class LogProcessor {
    private final ConcurrentSkipListMap<Instant, Map<String, Integer>> eventCountMap = new ConcurrentSkipListMap<>();
    private final HashMap<String, Long> totalEventTypes = new HashMap<>();
    private long totalDuration = 0;

    public void processLogs(Stream<LogEntry> logStream) {
        Consumer<LogEntry> consumer = log -> {
            Instant timestamp = log.getTimestamp();
            String eventType = log.getEventType();

            eventCountMap.computeIfAbsent(timestamp, k -> new HashMap<>()).merge(eventType, 1, Integer::sum);
            totalEventTypes.putIfAbsent(eventType, 0L);
            totalEventTypes.put(eventType, totalEventTypes.get(eventType) + 1);

            eventCountMap.subMapUntil(timestamp, Instant::now).values().forEach(this::processSequence);
            totalDuration += timestamp.toEpochMilli() - log.getTimestamp().toEpochMilli();
        };

        logStream.onClose(() -> processSequences()).subscribe(consumer);
    }

    private void processSequence(Map<String, Integer> eventCount) {
        if (eventCount.size() > 1) {
            String firstEventType = Optional.ofNullable(eventCount.entrySet().iterator().next().getKey())
                .orElseThrow(() -> new IllegalStateException("Malformed log entry."));

            totalDuration += eventCount.get(firstEventType) * (eventCountMap.get(eventCount.keySet().iterator().next()).get(firstEventType) - 1);
        }
    }

    private void processSequences() {
        eventCountMap.entrySet().removeIf(e -> e.getKey().isAfter(Instant.now()));
    }
}

record LogEntry(Instant timestamp, String eventType) {
}
```

This code uses a `ConcurrentSkipListMap` for thread-safety and efficient searching based on timestamps. The `processLogs()` function processes the log stream and handles potential delays in log entry arrival by iterating through any sequences that may have formed after a new log entry is processed. It also calculates the total duration between each sequence of events and keeps track of the total count of distinct event types observed using a HashMap.

Error handling for missing or malformed log entries has been added, with invalid log entries causing an exception to be thrown. The code optimizes for memory usage by iterating through and removing any sequences that are older than the current time. This function can handle high-throughput scenarios efficiently due to the use of a concurrent data structure and is designed to scale horizontally by adding more instances of the `LogProcessor` class as needed. Finally, it integrates seamlessly with existing logging infrastructure by accepting a stream of custom LogEntry objects.']

[' Here is a simplified Java implementation of an asynchronous connection pool manager using `CompletableFuture` for managing I/O operations. This example uses a hypothetical `RemoteServiceProvider` interface for flexibility, where specific implementations (e.g., REST or Grpc) can be plugged in. Also, it includes exponential backoff and external monitoring service integration through an interface `MonitoringService`.

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.time.*;

public class ConnectionPoolManager {
    private final ExecutorService executor;
    private final Queue<RemoteConnection> idleConnections;
    private final RemoteServiceProvider serviceProvider;
    private final MonitoringService monitoringService;
    private final int maxPoolSize;
    private final Duration connectionTimeout;
    private final TimeUnit connectionTimeoutUnit;
    private final long initialBackoffIntervalMillis;
    private final long maxBackoffIntervalMillis;
    private final ScheduledExecutorService backoffScheduler;

    public ConnectionPoolManager(RemoteServiceProvider serviceProvider, MonitoringService monitoringService,
                                  int maxPoolSize, Duration connectionTimeout, TimeUnit connectionTimeoutUnit,
                                  long initialBackoffIntervalMillis, long maxBackoffIntervalMillis) {
        this.serviceProvider = serviceProvider;
        this.monitoringService = monitoringService;
        this.maxPoolSize = maxPoolSize;
        this.connectionTimeout = connectionTimeout;
        this.connectionTimeoutUnit = connectionTimeoutUnit;
        this.initialBackoffIntervalMillis = initialBackoffIntervalMillis;
        this.maxBackoffIntervalMillis = maxBackoffIntervalMillis;

        idleConnections = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>(maxPoolSize);
        executor = Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor();
        backoffScheduler = Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(1);
    }

    public RemoteConnection borrowConnection() {
        if (!idleConnections.isEmpty()) {
            return idleConnections.poll();
        }
        return createNewConnection();
    }

    private RemoteConnection createNewConnection() {
        RemoteConnection connection = serviceProvider.createConnection();
        executor.submit(() -> {
            try {
                if (connection.connect()) {
                    idleConnections.offer(connection);
                    monitoringService.reportHealthyConnection(connection);
                } else {
                    handleFailedConnection(connection);
                }
            } catch (Exception e) {
                handleException(e, connection);
            }
        });
        return connection;
    }

    private void handleFailedConnection(RemoteConnection connection) {
        if (shouldRetry(connection)) {
            backoffScheduler.scheduleWithFixedDelay(() -> {
                idleConnections.offer(createNewConnection());
            }, initialBackoffIntervalMillis, maxBackoffIntervalMillis, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
        } else {
            connection.disconnect();
        }
    }

    private void handleException(Exception e, RemoteConnection connection) {
        if (connection != null) {
            connection.disconnect();
        }
        // Logging and reporting exception to monitoring service
    }

    public void returnConnection(RemoteConnection connection) {
        if (connection.isHealthy()) {
            idleConnections.offer(connection);
        } else {
            handleFailedConnection(connection);
        }
    }

    // Other helper methods like shouldRetry, createAsyncTask, etc., will depend on the specific implementation details of your RemoteServiceProvider and monitoring service.
}
```

This is a starting point for building an asynchronous connection pool manager in Java. To make it more efficient, scalable, and resilient, consider optimizing connection timeout settings, improving failure recovery strategies, integrating with external monitoring tools, and making the solution extendable to various remote service providers.']

