The total number of processed files is stored in a shared memory store, updated atomically to ensure thread safety in concurrent access scenarios. The solution also integrates an external metadata service for fetching additional attributes about the file, with fallback mechanisms in case of service unavailability.

For large-scale deployments, consider using a more efficient method for storing and updating the total number of processed files (e.g., Redis or MongoDB). Additionally, you may want to implement load balancing strategies when integrating with an external metadata service to handle high volumes of requests efficiently."]

