The function logs each successful memory allocation and initialization operation. It handles dynamic memory allocation failures gracefully, preventing partial allocations and ensuring no memory leaks occur.

It processes each file in the directory (you can implement processing logic for each file as per your requirements). The function renames each file by appending a unique identifier based on the file's creation time, size, and hash value. The new filename does not exceed a total length of 256 characters, including the directory path and the appended identifier.

The function cleans up all allocated resources when it exits to ensure no memory leaks occur. It documents that it makes assumptions about the logging framework implementation. You can further optimize this code based on your specific requirements and server environment constraints.']

